Change `WindowMetadataView.render` to `renderNode`, and it calls `content.render(env)` — but per the new contract, wrappers should call `content.renderNode(env)` for root-chain delegation. Since `WindowMetadataView` is a wrapper (a modifier), it should call `content.renderNode(env)` to keep the same component slot. If it calls `content.render(env)`, it creates a child slot and returns its node (aliasing). Our `renderView` aliasing check would throw if the child slot is in `renderingChildren`. The test stack shows it failed at `renderNode` because the method wasn't renamed. Fix:
```java
@Override
public PathlandNode renderNode(Environment env) {
    env.setWindowMetadata(metadata);
    return content.renderNode(env);
}
```
This matches the wrapper contract. Also check other new files from #167 that override `render` (WindowMetadata only? Search all `PathlandNode render(Environment` in main).

